From: chumby <chumby@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] label: take the scroll animation's path from its template too

A label's scroll animation takes its delay, repeats and completed
callback from the "anim" style's template, but not its path, so the
offset always moves smoothly, a pixel at a time: on a slow CPU each
pixel is a redraw of the whole label (~20 a second at 20 px/s), the
text rendered again each time. With the template's path (e.g. one that
steps every 100 ms) the label can scroll in fewer, bigger steps.

--- a/src/widgets/label/lv_label.c
+++ b/src/widgets/label/lv_label.c
@@ -1112,6 +1112,8 @@
             dest->repeat_delay = src->repeat_delay;
             dest->completed_cb = src->completed_cb;
             dest->reverse_delay = src->reverse_delay;
+            if(src->path_cb)
+                dest->path_cb = src->path_cb;
             break;
         case LV_LABEL_LONG_MODE_SCROLL_CIRCULAR:
             /* If the dest animation is already running, overwrite is not allowed */
@@ -1120,6 +1122,8 @@
             dest->repeat_cnt = src->repeat_cnt;
             dest->repeat_delay = src->repeat_delay;
             dest->completed_cb = src->completed_cb;
+            if(src->path_cb)
+                dest->path_cb = src->path_cb;
             break;
         default:
             break;
